2. Step-by-Step Deployment Setup (bash)

Run these commands on your Linode Compute instance (Nanode) to prepare the directories, virtual environment, and initial data seed:
bash
# 1. Create application directory and Python virtual environment
sudo mkdir -p /opt/binlog_sync
sudo chown "$USER:$USER" /opt/binlog_sync
python3 -m venv /opt/binlog_sync/venv
/opt/binlog_sync/venv/bin/pip install mysql-replication pymysql cryptography

# 2. Export initial allowlisted tables + exact binlog coordinate from source
mysqldump \
  --host=://aivencloud.com \
  --port=25060 \
  --user=avnadmin \
  --password \
  --ssl-mode=REQUIRED \
  --single-transaction \
  --set-gtid-purged=OFF \
  --master-data=2 \
  --hex-blob \
  app_db users orders order_items payments > /opt/binlog_sync/initial_seed.sql
Use code with caution.
(Load initial_seed.sql into each target database before starting the service.)

